export const FlakyTestItem = Schema.Struct({ "runner": Schema.suspend((): Schema.Codec<CITestRunnerEnum> => CITestRunnerEnum).annotate({ "description": "Test runner that emitted this signal: 'pytest' or 'jest'.\n\n* `pytest` - Pytest\n* `jest` - Jest" }), "nodeid": Schema.String.annotate({ "description": "Runner-specific stable test identity (the CI span name). This is a grouping key, not necessarily runnable; use `selector` to run or quarantine the test." }), "selector": Schema.String.annotate({ "description": "Runnable pytest or Jest selector. Exact when the CI reporter emitted it; older pytest spans use a best-effort reconstruction from the nodeid." }), "classification": Schema.suspend((): Schema.Codec<FlakyTestClassificationEnum> => FlakyTestClassificationEnum).annotate({ "description": "confirmed_flake: one commit both failed and passed the test (a re-run attempt went green, or an in-job retry recovered it), so it is provably nondeterministic. quarantined: a tolerated failure was recorded while it was masked. suspected_regression: only failures were recorded, which is absence of proof, not proof that it is a real break.\n\n* `confirmed_flake` - Confirmed Flake\n* `suspected_regression` - Suspected Regression\n* `quarantined` - Quarantined" }), "same_commit_recovery_run_count": Schema.Number.annotate({ "description": "Runs where one commit both failed and passed the test: a 'Re-run failed jobs' attempt went green on the same commit, or an in-job pytest retry (tests hand-marked @pytest.mark.flaky(reruns=N)) recovered it. A pass in a different run is a different commit and never counts." }).check(Schema.isInt().annotate({ "expected": "an integer" })), "failed_run_count": Schema.Number.annotate({ "description": "Distinct CI runs whose recorded outcome was failed or error. A run counts once however many matrix legs it failed in." }).check(Schema.isInt().annotate({ "expected": "an integer" })), "failed_pr_count": Schema.Number.annotate({ "description": "Distinct pull requests among the failed runs. Failures on master or unattributed branches carry no PR number and are excluded here (still in failed_run_count)." }).check(Schema.isInt().annotate({ "expected": "an integer" })), "master_failed_run_count": Schema.Number.annotate({ "description": "Failed runs on the default branch (master/main approximation): the 'matters right now' signal that a test is breaking the trunk, not just PR branches." }).check(Schema.isInt().annotate({ "expected": "an integer" })), "quarantined_failed_run_count": Schema.Number.annotate({ "description": "Runs where the test recorded a tolerated failure while quarantined: already masked in CI, still failing." }).check(Schema.isInt().annotate({ "expected": "an integer" })), "last_signal_at": Schema.String.annotate({ "description": "Most recent failure, recovery, or quarantined-failure run for this test in the window.", "format": "date-time" }) }).annotate({ "identifier": "FlakyTestItem" })
