export const CohortRealtimeReadiness = Schema.Struct({ "state": Schema.suspend((): Schema.Codec<CohortRealtimeStateEnum> => CohortRealtimeStateEnum).annotate({ "description": "Whether feature flags can target this cohort now. `ready`: they can, and they see membership changes within about a minute. `building` / `rebuilding`: PostHog is preparing the cohort from past events, and flags cannot target it yet. `needs_attention`: the cohort qualifies but nothing is preparing it. `daily`: its criteria are not supported in realtime, so its membership only comes from the once-a-day calculation. `person_properties`: it matches on person properties, which flags read directly, so they can always target it. `static`: it is a fixed list of people.\n\n* `static` - Static\n* `person_properties` - Person properties\n* `daily` - Daily\n* `building` - Building\n* `rebuilding` - Rebuilding\n* `ready` - Ready\n* `needs_attention` - Needs attention" }), "ready_at": Schema.Union([Schema.String, Schema.Null]).annotate({ "description": "When the cohort became targetable by feature flags. Null unless the state is `ready`.", "format": "date-time" }), "build": Schema.Union([CohortHistoryBuild, Schema.Null], { mode: "oneOf" }).annotate({ "description": "The build preparing the cohort. Null unless the state is `building` or `rebuilding`." }), "reason": Schema.Union([CohortRealtimeUnavailableReasonEnum, NullEnum], { mode: "oneOf" }).annotate({ "description": "Why feature flags can't target the cohort. `history_over_limit`, on a `daily` cohort: its criteria look back further than `history_limit_days`. `too_large_to_build`, on a `needs_attention` cohort: the events in its criteria happen too often for PostHog to prepare it automatically. Null in every other case, including a `daily` cohort that other criteria keep off realtime.\n\n* `history_over_limit` - History over limit\n* `too_large_to_build` - Too large to build" }), "history_limit_days": Schema.Union([Schema.Int, Schema.Null]).annotate({ "description": "The most days realtime cohort criteria can look back. Null unless the reason is `history_over_limit`." }) }).annotate({ "identifier": "CohortRealtimeReadiness" })
